# cli
- label: the CLI supports --config, --port, --preset/-P, --list-presets, --help, --version; unknown commands or options cause immediate exit with usage
  command: bun run src/cli.ts --help 2>&1 | grep -q "Usage:" && bun run src/cli.ts badcmd 2>&1 | grep -q "Unknown command"
  tags: [implemented]
- label: the CLI always chdirs to its own project root (package.json dir) before starting to ensure tsconfig, defaults and data/ are found regardless of invocation cwd
  command: grep -q "process.chdir(projectRoot)" src/cli.ts && grep -q "projectRoot = join(import.meta.dir, \"..\")" src/cli.ts
  tags: [implemented]
- label: CLI supports --preset <name> / -P <name> and --list-presets for bundled presets
  command: bun run src/cli.ts --list-presets 2>&1 | grep -q tech-news && bun run src/cli.ts --help 2>&1 | grep -q 'preset <name>'
  tags: [spec, implemented]

## chdir
- CLI supports -C/--chdir <dir> (after td2 projectRoot bootstrap chdir); user dir (abs or rel to invocation cwd) is chdir'ed to so subsequent config/preset/port validation + data/ loads + server run use it; invalid/nonexistent dir -> clean error 'Failed to chdir to <target>: <cause>' + exit 1 (no crash/stack); unknown opt no longer for --chdir; covered by new TDD test in cli.test.ts (spawn with valid tmp + bad dir cases exercising early error and continued validation) @implemented

# config
- when no config file is present, loadConfig falls back to config.example.yaml then a default layout with a single 'all' panel
- config errors are always prefixed with 'config: ' and cause the process to exit 1 before the server starts
- AppConfig validation is exhaustive and path-specific: unknown top-level keys, missing required fields, invalid numbers/enums, duplicate names/IDs, bad pipeline source refs, and partial LLM creds all produce precise 'config: ...' errors at load time
- the special source value 'all' (and panels using it) bypasses adapter/pipeline name validation and sourceToPanels mapping; it queries global recent items instead of per-panel
- Panel IDs are stable 8-character hex (first of sha256 of JSON.stringify({panel, source, limit})) or explicit id from config; used for DB keys, refresh URLs, and sourceToPanels mapping
- environment variables in the form ${VAR} are recursively substituted in all string values of the YAML (including in llm.api_key, adapter params, etc.) before schema validation
- label: loadConfig resolves bare short preset names (tech-news, ml-ai, etc) to bundled /app/presets/config.*.yaml
  command: bun run src/cli.ts --preset tech-news --help 2>&1 | grep -q 'pace v'
  tags: [spec, implemented]

## env
- loadConfig performs recursive ${VAR} substitution (chained env values containing further ${REF} are fully expanded in all YAML string fields e.g. adapter params, llm.api_key before validation; includes depth guard preventing infinite recursion on cycles) + config.test.ts regression test for it (directly makes wyp true + strengthens 0g1 exhaustive quality) @implemented

# scheduler
- scheduler errors for missing adapter types are prefixed 'scheduler: ' and cause startup to fail with exit 1
- the Scheduler starts an immediate fetch for each configured adapter on startup; pipelines are scheduled with a 5s initial delay; default refresh_interval is 15 minutes (minimum 1)

## startup
- scheduler.test.ts contains a regression test for t3i: pipelines scheduled with 5s initial delay before first run (using exported PIPELINE_INITIAL_DELAY_MS=5000 const); adapters fetch immediate on start; default refresh 15m (min 1) when omitted; the const provides assertable hook and clarifies magic number in startup logic @implemented

# server
- label: the server listens on port 7453 by default (or PORT env / --port); supports graceful shutdown on SIGTERM/SIGINT (stops scheduler, closes DB)
  command: grep -q "parsePort(process.env.PORT, 7453)" src/index.ts
- manual refresh via POST /refresh/:panel returns 502 with details if any source in the batch fails; success redirects to / with 303
- every response includes security headers: X-Content-Type-Options nosniff, X-Frame-Options DENY, Referrer-Policy strict-origin-when-cross-origin, CSP default-src self with unsafe-inline for styles
- GET /health returns JSON {status: "ok"}; GET /styles.css serves the static CSS with 1h cache

## headers
- server responses include /health 200+JSON {status:"ok"} (m15), /styles.css 200+public max-age=3600 cache (m15), /refresh/:panel 502 w/ "Refresh failed for ..." details when sources fail e.g. reddit (igb) + 404 unknown + 303 success, and ALL responses (200/404/502) include yn0 headers (X-Content-Type-Options nosniff, X-Frame-Options DENY, Referrer-Policy, CSP default-src 'self' + style-src unsafe-inline) PLUS Permissions-Policy: interest-cohort=() (quality security hardening); integration test in cli.test.ts using bg spawn+fetch --preset tech-news (TDD red-green on header addition) @implemented

# adapters
- every Adapter must export a default object with .name (string) and .fetch(config: AdapterConfig): Promise<ContentItem[]>; discovery scans src/adapters/*.ts at runtime (excludes tests/types/index)
- Adapter fetch implementations that encounter network/HTTP/parse errors either throw (with `${name}: ` prefix + errorMessage) or console.warn and return []; the contract in types.ts documents the expectation for callers
- ContentItem ids are prefixed by adapter (e.g. 'hn:', 'rss:', 'github:') or 'pipeline:${name}:' to avoid collisions across sources; used as DB PK for upsert
- every ContentItem.timestamp is a valid Date (parse failures or missing dates fall back to new Date())

## errorMessage
- errorMessage helper returns the .message property for plain objects with .message (duck type support after Error check) enabling robust cause strings in adapter fetch error throws/warns of form `: ...${errorMessage(err)}` per mmu contract and types.ts JSDoc (TDD test added for network/parse error obj shapes) @implemented

